      "body": "## What the official source states\nThe Federal Reserve Board on Tuesday released the minutes from its recent meetings to review and determine the discount rates provided to depository institutions through the discount window. Today's minutes cover the Board meetings that occurred on August 17, September 9, and September 16, 2026. [source:873093a8-085e-42b5-8bb2-657f62f8df94]\n\n## How to read the reported information\nThe Board's process for setting the discount rate is distinct from the process the Federal Open Market Committee follows in setting the target range for the federal funds rate. [source:873093a8-085e-42b5-8bb2-657f62f8df94]\n\n## Limits and source context\nThe minutes provide a record of the discussions and decisions made during the Board's discount rate meetings. The information is limited to the details provided in the official release and does not include additional commentary or analysis. [source:873093a8-085e-42b5-8bb2-657f62f8df94]",
